          },
          {
            "id": 586,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-QwDpdqgK7o2hSlxVBAjl7U5TgWu\">On the western side of the library five years ago, there were three main areas: a classroom at the top, a meeting room in the middle, and a borrowing and returning desk at the bottom. In the current layout, the classroom has been converted into a recording studio, while the meeting room remains in its original position. However, the borrowing and returning functions have been separated into two distinct areas.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13834,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 587,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-U4zqdvQhRobDCexOQwqlbeyCgPg\">Regarding the eastern and central section, the library office that was present five years ago has been replaced by a conference room. There were desks for computers 5 years ago, but they have been repurposed to store students' laptops. Additionally, in the central area, the original studying tables have been transformed into private studying tables, and a new desk specifically for students' laptops has been installed below them.</div>\n</div>",
